  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening CAFOD&#x2019;s approach to peacebuilding in Lebanon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In 2015, in recognition of the protracted nature of the Syria crisis and in response to a CAFOD 2-year investment in peacebuilding in the Middle East, CAFOD began to expand its programme of long-term development work in Lebanon beyond support to Palestinian refugees and migrant workers and sought out new partnerships.  CAFOD&#x2019;s Syria crisis emergency response programme also initiated new partnerships which included peacebuilding components.   Now with 2-years&#x2019; experience of supporting local, community-based peacebuilding initiatives, CAFOD is commissioning a piece of research to consolidate the learning from this programming, reassess and evaluate the validity of our peacebuilding strategy, deepen our context and conflict analysis and explore how this work can be strengthened particularly in relation to Monitoring, Evaluation and Learning.</narrative>
  </description>
